#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:2
msgid "Unofficial and unmaintained projects policy"
msgstr "非官方与无人维护项目政策"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:4
msgid ""
"This policy describes a process where we take actions against unmaintained_ "
"and unofficial_ forks of project documentation."
msgstr "本政策描述我们对项目文档的 unmaintained_ 和 unofficial_ fork 采取措施的流程。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:6
msgid ""
"If you want to free up a project's :term:`slug` and gain access over it, "
"please see :doc:`/abandoned-projects`."
msgstr "若你想释放某项目的 :term:`slug` 并取得其控制权，请参阅 :doc:`/abandoned-projects` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:9
msgid "Rationale"
msgstr "制定依据"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:11
msgid ""
"Documentation projects may be kept online indefinitely, even though a newer "
"version of the same project exists elsewhere. There are many reasons this "
"can happen, including forks, old official docs that are unmaintained, and "
"many other situations."
msgstr "文档项目可能长期在线，即便同一项目已有更新版本存在于别处。造成这种情况的原因很多，包括 fork、无人维护的旧官方文档，以及许多其他情形。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:15
msgid ""
"The problem with old, outdated docs is that users will find them in search "
"results, and get confused to the validity of them. Projects will then get "
"support requests from people who are using an old and incorrect "
"documentation version."
msgstr "过时文档的问题在于用户会在搜索结果中找到它们，并对其有效性感到困惑。随后项目会收到来自使用旧版错误文档用户的支持请求。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:19
msgid ""
"We have this policy to allow a reporter to request the *delisting* of forks "
"that are old and outdated."
msgstr "我们制定本政策，让报告者可以请求将陈旧过时的 fork *从列表中移除* 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:23
msgid "High level overview"
msgstr "高层概览"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:25
msgid "The process at a high level looks like:"
msgstr "流程的高层结构如下："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:27
msgid "A reporter contacts us about a project they think is outdated and unofficial"
msgstr "报告者就他们认为过时且非官方的项目联系我们"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:28
msgid ""
"A Read the Docs team member evaluates it to make sure it's outdated and "
"unofficial, according to this policy"
msgstr "Read the Docs 团队成员依据本政策评估，确认其确实过时且非官方"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:29
msgid ""
"We delist this project from search results and send an email to owners of "
"the Read the Docs project"
msgstr "我们将其从搜索结果中移除，并向 Read the Docs 项目所有者发送邮件"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:30
msgid ""
"If a project owner objects, we evaluate their evidence and make a final "
"decision"
msgstr "若项目所有者提出异议，我们评估其证据并作出最终决定"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:34
msgid "Definitions"
msgstr "定义"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:38
msgid "Unofficial projects"
msgstr "非官方项目"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:40
msgid ""
"A project is considered *unofficial* when it is not linked to or mentioned "
"in **any** of these places:"
msgstr "当项目未在**以下任何一处** 被链接或提及时，视为*非官方* ："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:42
msgid "Websites and domains associated with the project"
msgstr "与项目关联的网站和域名"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:43
msgid ""
"The project's primary repository -- README files, repository description, or"
" source code"
msgstr "项目的主仓库——README 文件、仓库描述或源代码"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:47
msgid "Unmaintained projects"
msgstr "无人维护的项目"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:49
msgid "A project is considered *unmaintained* when **any** of the following are met:"
msgstr "当满足以下**任一** 条件时，项目被视为*无人维护* ："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:51
msgid ""
"The configured version control repository is unreadable. This can happen if "
"the repository is deleted, credentials are broken or the Git host is "
"permanently unresponsive."
msgstr "配置的版本控制仓库不可读。可能因仓库被删除、凭据失效或 Git 主机长期无响应而发生。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:52
msgid ""
"The project is only serving content from releases and commits 6 months or "
"older."
msgstr "项目只提供 6 个月或更早的发布与提交内容。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:53
msgid "All builds have failed for more than 6 months."
msgstr "所有构建已失败超过 6 个月。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:57
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr "实施"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:61
msgid "Requesting a project be delisted"
msgstr "请求将项目从列表移除"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:63
msgid ""
"You can request that we delist an outdated, unmaintained documentation by "
"contacting our :doc:`/support`."
msgstr "你可以联系我们的 :doc:`/support` ，请求我们移除过时且无人维护的文档。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:65
msgid "Please include the following information:"
msgstr "请包含以下信息："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:79
msgid "Delisting"
msgstr "从列表移除"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:81
msgid ""
"Projects that are determined to be unmaintained_ and unofficial_ will have a"
" ``robots.txt`` file added that removes them from all search results:"
msgstr "被判定为 unmaintained_ 且 unofficial_ 的项目将被添加 ``robots.txt`` 文件，从所有搜索结果中移除："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:92
msgid "Projects will be delisted if they meet **all** of the following criteria:"
msgstr "项目满足以下**全部** 标准时会被从列表移除："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:94
msgid ""
"The person who submits the report of the unmaintained_ and unofficial_ "
"project also demonstrates failed attempts to contact the existing owners."
msgstr "提交 unmaintained_ 且 unofficial_ 项目报告的人，同时证明曾尝试联系现有所有者但未果。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:95
msgid ""
"The project has been determined unmaintained_ and unofficial_ by the rules "
"described above."
msgstr "项目已依据上述规则被判定为 unmaintained_ 且 unofficial_。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:96
msgid "The core team does not have any additional reservations."
msgstr "核心团队没有其他顾虑。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:98
msgid ""
"The Read the Docs team will do the following actions when a project is "
"delisted:"
msgstr "项目被从列表移除时，Read the Docs 团队将执行以下操作："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:100
msgid "Notify the Read the Docs project owners via email about the delisting."
msgstr "通过邮件通知 Read the Docs 项目所有者该移除决定。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:101
msgid "Add the ``robots.txt`` file to be served on the project domain."
msgstr "添加 ``robots.txt`` 文件在项目域名上提供服务。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:103
msgid ""
"If any of the project owners respond, their response will be taken into "
"account, and the delisting might be reversed."
msgstr "若有任何项目所有者回应，其意见将被纳入考虑，移除决定可能被撤销。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:107
msgid "Thinking behind the policy"
msgstr "政策背后的考量"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:109
msgid ""
"The main idea behind this policy is that Read the Docs serves the community."
" Every user is invited to upload content under `terms of service "
"<https://about.readthedocs.com/terms-of-service/>`_ understanding that it is"
" at the sole risk of the user."
msgstr ""
"本政策背后的核心思想是：Read the Docs 服务于社区。每位用户都受 `terms of service "
"<https://about.readthedocs.com/terms-of-service/>`_ 邀请上传内容，并理解这完全由用户自行承担风险。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:113
msgid ""
"While Read the Docs is not a backup service, the core team of Read the Docs "
"does their best to keep content accessible indefinitely in its published "
"form. However, in certain edge cases, the greater community's needs might "
"outweigh the individual's expectation of continued publishing."
msgstr ""
"虽然 Read the Docs "
"并非备份服务，但其核心团队会尽力让内容以已发布的形式长期可访问。然而在某些边缘情况下，更广泛的社区需求可能优先于个人对持续发布的期待。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:118
msgid "Prior art"
msgstr "先例"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/unofficial-projects.rst:120
msgid ""
"This policy is inspired by our :doc:`abandoned-projects`. The Python Package"
" Index (PyPI) policy for claiming abandoned packages (`PEP-0541 "
"<https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0541>`_) heavily influenced this "
"policy."
msgstr ""
"本政策受我们的 :doc:`abandoned-projects` 启发。Python 包索引（PyPI）关于认领废弃包的政策（`PEP-0541 "
"<https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0541>`_ ）对本政策影响深远。"

